---
import ModelFacts from '../../../../components/ModelFacts.astro';
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/ai.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Kimi K3.1 Pro (Moonshot) - A.I. - Rycode"
  description="Kimi K3.1 Pro is Moonshot AI's post-trained version of Kimi K3, released 23 Oct 2026 on the Kimi API. 1,048,576-token context. Moonshot says full weights ship by 4 Nov 2026."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">Open weight · weights due by 4 Nov</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Kimi K3.1 Pro (Moonshot)</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">Kimi K3.1 Pro is Moonshot AI's updated version of <a href="/ai/models/open-weight/kimi-k3/">Kimi K3</a>, released on <strong>23 Oct 2026</strong>. Moonshot calls it the first model in its K3.1 series. The full weights are due by <strong>4 Nov 2026</strong>, so for now it runs only through Moonshot's API and apps.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />
    <ModelFacts />
    <p>Kimi K3.1 Pro is Moonshot AI's updated version of Kimi K3, released on 23 Oct 2026 according to <a href="https://openrouter.ai/moonshotai/kimi-k3.1-pro">Kimi K3.1 Pro on OpenRouter</a> [1]. Moonshot's <a href="https://www.kimi.ai/blog/kimi-k3-1-pro">Kimi K3.1 Pro Tech Blog</a> calls it a post-trained version of K3, which means the same base model given more training after its first training run [2]. It has a 1,048,576-token context window, which is how much text it can read in one request, per Moonshot's <a href="https://platform.kimi.ai/docs/pricing/chat">Model Inference Pricing Explanation</a> [3].</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Benchmarking</h2>
    <p>The cells below are Moonshot's 24 Oct 2026 tech blog. They are lab claims on Moonshot harnesses unless noted.</p>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table ai-model-table--prose">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Eval</th>
            <th scope="col">Kimi K3.1 Pro</th>
            <th scope="col">Notes</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Terminal-Bench 4.0</td><td>65.7%</td><td>Lab claim. Ahead of GPT-6 Astra (58.2%); behind Claude Opus 5.5 (66.4%).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Kimi Code Bench 3.0 Long-horizon</td><td>61.2%</td><td>Lab claim. Internal benchmark; K3 scored 55.95%.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>BenchCAD (with tools)</td><td>92.7%</td><td>Lab claim. 3D reconstruction via CAD code; Moonshot cites Claude Opus 5.5 at 96.2% and GPT-6 Astra at 95.9% on the same chart.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Kimi Hallu Bench Hard (claim-level)</td><td>8.3%</td><td>Lab claim. Hallucination rate on a stress-test set; K3 was 23.4%. Lower is better.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Access and price</h2>
    <p>On the Kimi API it is <code>kimi-k3.1-pro</code> at $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens, and <code>kimi-k3.1-pro-highspeed</code> costs $4 and $20 [3]. Moonshot says Highspeed runs at two to three times the speed of K3.1 Pro [2]. Moonshot lists it on Kimi.ai, Kimi Work, Kimi Code, and the Kimi API [2].</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Weights</h2>
    <p>The blog says the full weights will be released by 4 Nov 2026, so for now it runs only through Moonshot's API and apps [2]. Until then, the open weights on this site are Kimi K3's: <a href="https://huggingface.co/moonshotai/Kimi-K3">moonshotai/Kimi-K3</a>.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Sources</h2>
    <ol class="ai-model-sources">
      <li><a href="https://openrouter.ai/moonshotai/kimi-k3.1-pro">Kimi K3.1 Pro - API Pricing &amp; Benchmarks | OpenRouter</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.kimi.ai/blog/kimi-k3-1-pro">Kimi K3.1 Pro Tech Blog: Advancing Open Intelligence</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://platform.kimi.ai/docs/pricing/chat">Model Inference Pricing Explanation - Kimi API Platform</a></li>
    </ol>
  </article>
</Layout>
